# The two names everything else derives from.
#
# Sourced by setup-ingress.sh, setup-turn.sh, verify-live.sh, farm-online.sh and farm-check.sh, so
# moving the farm to a domain is an edit HERE and nowhere else. Before this file existed the console
# hostname was hardcoded in seven places and the relay address in two, which meant a rename was nine
# edits and one of them would be missed.
#
# Committed on purpose: neither value is a secret, both are public DNS, and a checked-in default is
# what makes `farm-check.sh` work on a fresh clone without setup. Secrets live in deploy/secrets/.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the console
# Serves the console, /v1, the WebDriver hub, and /dp (the live-view socket). Caddy terminates TLS
# here and it is the ONLY public listener on the control plane.
#
# Pinned to the reserved address `mfarm-lab-ip` (34.100.138.213 — the name is historically wrong,
# see below). sslip.io resolves the dashed form to that IP by construction, so it needs no DNS and
# survives a stop/start now that the address is reserved.
MFARM_PUBLIC_HOST=34-100-138-213.sslip.io

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the media relay
# coturn on the DEVICE host. The only thing that host publishes: no console, no API, no adb.
#
# Pinned to the reserved address `mfarm-ip` (34.100.159.34). An IP rather than a name today; it
# becomes turn.<domain> when DNS moves, and that is the whole change.
MFARM_TURN_HOST=34.100.159.34

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- naming, because it will confuse
# THE TWO RESERVED ADDRESSES ARE NAMED BACKWARDS, and it is not a mistake anyone can safely fix:
#
#   mfarm-lab-ip  34.100.138.213  ->  mfarm-cp   (the CONTROL PLANE)
#   mfarm-ip      34.100.159.34   ->  mfarm-lab  (the DEVICE HOST)
#
# Both names date from the single-box era. GCP cannot rename a reserved address — you release and
# re-reserve, and a release hands the address back to the pool where somebody else may take it. The
# console URL and its certificate both depend on 34.100.138.213 keeping that exact value, so the
# names stay wrong and this comment exists instead.
